WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.199
Good morning, Hank, it’s Tuesday.

00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:04.700
I’m doing a photoshoot in which they want
me to pretend to vlog so I’m going to actually

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:05.700
vlog.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.700
Here are all the people taking my picture.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.720
Woke up in Los Angeles at 6:15 in the morning
on Saturday, brushed my teeth, got my picture

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:13.820
taken while taking moving pictures of myself,
and then got on a hotel elevator clearly not

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.500
designed for people who fear heights.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.810
I don’t like this at all.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:20.820
Met up with Eleanor &amp; Park author Rainbow
Rowell and then went to USC for the L.A. Times

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.660
book festival where my long time editor Julie
Strauss-Gabel was talking to Maya Van Wagenen,

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:29.090
a 15-year-old who has written a fascinating
and wonderful anthropological experiment/memoir

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.090
called Popular.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:33.400
And then I got to ride in a golf cart - you
can just see my glee - before heading backstage

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.539
to prepare for my event.

00:00:34.539 --> 00:00:38.579
I was very nervous backstage, but man, the
lighting was fantastic.

00:00:38.579 --> 00:00:42.399
Hank, before I go on stage for book stuff
now, I always remind myself of my readings,

00:00:42.399 --> 00:00:46.800
and there were many of them, that were attended
by between 0 and 3 people, and I give thanks

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:51.359
for Brotherhood 2.0 and Nerdfighteria and
for you, Hank, and then I take a deep breath

00:00:51.359 --> 00:00:56.829
and, well… (crowd cheering)

00:00:56.829 --> 00:01:01.859
So I talked to all these nice people for a
while, and then went over to sign books for

00:01:01.859 --> 00:01:06.500
several hours where I met lots of people wearing
various "okay, okay" shirts, and TFIOS iPhone

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.470
cases, and TFIOS nails, and a dog named Alaska,
and this couple who met through Nerdfighteria

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:12.940
and now are married.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:15.861
Then I met up with my friend Veronica Roth,
and shortly thereafter, fell asleep in the

00:01:15.861 --> 00:01:17.500
cab on the way back to the hotel.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:22.390
I was trying to film myself fake falling asleep,
but then I actually fell asleep, so it goes…

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:26.300
Woke up the next morning at 5:15 to watch
Liverpool - Manchester City, which was wonderful,

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.380
and then terrifying, and then wonderful again.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:30.380
Yes!

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:31.590
We did it, Hank.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:37.240
We being, of course, the people on the pitch,
the people in the stadium, and me in Los Angeles

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:38.640
wearing my Liverpool jacket.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.770
And then I got to see my friend T Cooper who
wrote Changers, and then I headed to different

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:42.770
hotel to meet…

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:46.360
Oh, look, it’s Ansel Elgort, who plays Gus
in The Fault in Our Stars, and whose worldview

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:50.820
involves a great deal of shirtlessness, and
frankly, who among us can blame him?

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:53.981
Sarah was there too and we drank champagne
by the pool which was awesome, and then we

00:01:53.981 --> 00:01:57.890
got all fancy for the MTV Movie Awards, met
up with Nat Wolff, and soon found ourselves

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:59.600
on an actual red carpet.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:03.420
Hank, I really love Nerdfighteria and the
chance to talk about stuff I care about with

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:07.270
people I care about, but I don’t particularly
wanna be, like, a real celebrity, which is

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:10.950
why we've always turned down TV stuff, but
I’m really proud of the TFIOS movie and

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:14.129
I want to support it, and plus I like hanging
out with Nat, so there we were on the very

00:02:14.129 --> 00:02:16.920
same red carpet as, like, Jonah Hill and Grumpy
Cat.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:20.650
Nat and I tried to answer questions even though
the screaming and the cameras resulted in

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:24.280
both of us, to use internet parlance, losing
our ability to even.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:28.260
It was really, really overwhelming, Hank,
and interviewers kept asking me how I was

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:31.409
handling the attention that accompanies a
book becoming a movie and if our community

00:02:31.409 --> 00:02:34.430
would change because of it, and I wanted to
answer every question by saying “I AM FREAKING

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:35.430
OUT RIGHT NOW!”

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:40.180
And I found myself thinking of Grumpy Cat,
who, in spite of it all, remained, you know,

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:42.680
cat-like, and grumpy, and I thought: “You
know what?

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.859
Grumpy Cat has this thing figured out!”

00:02:44.859 --> 00:02:48.439
So Nerdfighteria, this is gonna be weird and
hopefully awesome, but let’s just focus

00:02:48.439 --> 00:02:51.700
on continuing to do the stuff that we're good
at, okay?

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:52.700
And on that subject:

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:53.700
Hi, Hank.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:54.700
Me from the future here.

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.010
In a stunning turn of events, I find myself
in an airport.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:59.840
Anyway, we are relaunching the Nerdfighter
Book Club, and our new book is going to be

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:03.799
Behind the Beautiful Forevers, by Katherine
Boo, a fascinating and nuanced look at poverty

00:03:03.799 --> 00:03:06.519
in one Indian community, so check it out;
link's in the doobly-doo.

